THIRD-PARTY NOTICES

This repository contains NO third-party source code.

`bin/jointstd/` is an independent, stdlib-only implementation of the community
measurement standard proposed by brandonmusic (Brandon M. Music). His harness
(`kld_eval`) is distributed under the SHAPLEYMCG LICENSE 1.0, a source-available
licence; no line of it is copied here. `bin/jointstd/oracle.py` OPTIONALLY
IMPORTS his analysis layer, when the user has installed it themselves, to use as
a validation oracle against our own implementation. The known-answer fixture at
`bin/jointstd/fixtures/brandonmusic-known-answer.json` reproduces MEASUREMENT
RESULTS he published — numbers, with attribution — not code.

Measurements in this repository are made against panels and teacher logits
published by brandonmusic, and against base models published by Z.ai (zai-org).
Trellis codec kernels referenced by the quantization tooling are by turboderp
(exllamav3, MIT). Each is credited at its point of use.
